POSTERIFLOW — SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
=================================

PosteriFlow estimates, in one forward pass, the posterior over 11 parameters
of the k-th loudest compact-binary signal in 4 s of whitened H1/L1/V1 strain.

  parameters (fixed order): mass_1, mass_2, luminosity_distance, ra, dec,
                            theta_jn, psi, phase, geocent_time, a1, a2


1. END-TO-END FLOW
------------------

  configs/*.yaml
        │
        ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────┐   src/ahsd/data/
  │ DATA GENERATION (bilby)      │   parameter_sampler → waveform → project onto
  │ components stored separately │   H1/L1/V1 → whiten → store noise and every
  └──────────────┬───────────────┘   signal as its own float16 component
                 ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────┐   scripts/audit_dataset.py
  │ AUDIT                        │   ranges, class mix, distance shape, SNR,
  └──────────────┬───────────────┘   no wrapped inspirals, duplicates, noise stats
                 ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────┐   experiments/remix_data.py
  │ REMIX (every epoch)          │   fresh example per event per epoch
  └──────────────┬───────────────┘
                 ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────┐   experiments/train_lean_npe.py
  │ TRAIN LeanNPE (pure NLL)     │   calibration-gated checkpoint selection
  └──────────────┬───────────────┘
                 ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────┐   scripts/validate_checkpoint.py
  │ CERTIFY                      │   SBC, coverage, railing, real GWTC events
  └──────────────┬───────────────┘   of the model's classes → HTML report
                 ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────┐   src/ahsd/inference/, infer.py
  │ INFERENCE                    │   preprocessing → posterior → gating →
  └──────────────────────────────┘   importance reweighting / dynesty fallback

  On the cluster, scripts/run_pipeline.py chains all of the above (SLURM jobs:
  generate → audit → train → certify → summary) for the four models.


2. DATA GENERATION — src/ahsd/data/
-----------------------------------

  sample_signal_parameters      masses, spins, sky, orientation, distance
                                (uniform-in-distance per class), merger time
  BilbyWaveformGenerator        IMRPhenomXP (BBH), IMRPhenomNSBH (NSBH),
                                IMRPhenomD_NRTidalv2 (BNS). Signals that
                                fit the 4 s window are generated directly;
                                longer inspirals (all BNS/NSBH, light BBH) are
                                generated over a longer power-of-two segment
                                starting a few seconds before the window
  BilbySignalInjector           antenna-pattern projection + time delays
  BilbyPreprocessor             whitening by the design PSD; long signals are
                                whitened on the long segment, then cropped
  DatasetGenerator              events of 1–5 signals (overlap_fraction),
                                SNR cut on the loudest, train/val/test splits
  generate_parallel.py          independent seeded shards merged into one
                                dataset; build_memmap_cache → memmap/ per split

  Storage per event: one whitened noise realization + each whitened signal
  component + its 11 labels. Network SNR = L2 norm of the whitened signal.

  Datasets:  dataset_v3       mixed BBH/NSBH/BNS   (data_config_fixed.yaml)
             dataset_bbh_v3   BBH only             (data_config_bbh_v3.yaml)
             dataset_nsbh_v3  NSBH only            (data_config_nsbh_v3.yaml)
             dataset_bns_v3   BNS only             (data_config_bns_v3.yaml)


3. REMIX — experiments/remix_data.py
------------------------------------

  RemixDataset assembles a new example from the stored components each epoch:

  noise swap            any stored Gaussian realization
  real noise            O2/O3 GWOSC crops (data/noise_bank); signals re-colored
                        exactly: irfft(rfft(sig) · ASD_design / ASD_measured)
  time shift            common circular roll           → geocent_time updated
  distance rescale      amplitude × s                  → d_L ÷ s
  overlap summation     signals summed, re-sorted by loudness Mc^(5/6)/d_L
  detector dropout      dropped detector → unit white noise
  delay/sky remap       experiments/delay_aug.py: sky moved to a scored
                        candidate, per-detector delays/antenna factors applied,
                        distance kept inside the model support

  Returns (strain [3,16384], params [5,11], n_signals, net_snr, asd_bands).
  persistent_workers=False so set_epoch() reaches the loader workers.


4. MODEL — src/ahsd/models/
---------------------------

  LeanNPE (lean_npe.py)

  whitened strain [B, 3, 16384]
     │
     ├─► asinh ─► conv stem (4 strided Conv1d, no normalization) ─► d_model 192
     │            + detector embedding + sinusoidal positions
     │
     ├─► CoherentEncoder branches, injected as tokens into the transformer
     │     geometry      power-weighted complex coherence |γ|, phase per band,
     │                   GCC arrival-time delays              → 4 tokens
     │     MF tokens     per-detector complex overlaps with a fixed (Mc, q)
     │     (--mf_tokens) template bank (assets/mf_bank_*.npz), alias-free
     │                   band-limited IFFT; gated into the geometry slots
     │     polarization  polarization_features.py: best network-SNR template,
     │     (--pol_features)  per detector pair log|z_I/z_J|, cos/sin Δφ, Δt,
     │                   per detector asinh SNR (15 values)   → 2 tokens
     │
     ├─► 3-layer pre-norm transformer (6 heads) ─► attention pooling (8 queries)
     ├─► log-energy branch: 16 windowed log-energies of the raw strain
     ├─► PSD branch (--psd_cond): per-detector log-ASD vs design in 16 bands
     │
     ▼
  context (256) ⊕ rank embedding (32, up to 5 signals)
     ▼
  NSFPosteriorFlow (flows.py, nflows): 10 layers, 256 hidden, 16 bins
     ▼
  11-D posterior in [-1, 1]  ─► ParamScaler ─► physical units

  ParamScaler: fixed map, log for masses/distance; mass coordinates mc_q
  (chirp mass, mass ratio); circular ra/phase/psi wrap at sampling; the
  distance support (dist_range) is a buffer stored in the checkpoint.

  Per-class choices
    BBH, mixed   coherent + MF tokens (mf_bank_bbh.npz) + polarization tokens
    NSBH, BNS    coherent encoder without template tokens

  Checkpoint: best_model.pth = {model_state_dict, args, epoch, val_nll,
  diagnostics}. Load with ahsd.inference.pipeline.load_model(), which rebuilds
  LeanNPE from args (every constructor flag must be read there and at every
  other load site).


5. TRAINING — experiments/train_lean_npe.py
-------------------------------------------

  loss            NLL of the flow (+ optional --aux_mass regression on the
                  encoder context)
  validation      fixed Gaussian and real-noise validation sets each epoch;
                  selection metric = their mean
  per-epoch       shufΔ (context-shuffle NLL rise), dcorr, dcov50/90, spurious
  diagnostics     railing, base concentration, high-SNR coverage, SBC, corner
                  table, basin probe (BBH models)
  selection       best_model.pth = lowest selection metric among epochs with
                  spurious railing ≤ --max_spurious_railing; last_model.pth and
                  epoch_XXXX.pth are always written


6. INFERENCE — src/ahsd/inference/
----------------------------------

  pipeline.infer()       GWOSC event / local strain / injection
     preprocessing       fetch, whiten with the measured PSD, compute asd_bands
     resolve_model       class model (CLASS_MODELS) for --event-type, else mixed
     sample              LeanNPE.sample_posterior(rank=k)
     ood / gating        context OOD score + railing + width → confidence;
                         refinement gate flags known hard regions
     importance          likelihood importance reweighting
     dynesty_bridge      full sampler for events flagged LOW confidence
     result              PosteriorResult: median, intervals, diagnostics,
                         distance-prior reweighting, plots

  infer_overlapping()    one query per rank; optional PriorityNet
                         (src/ahsd/core/priority_net.py) reorders the results


7. VALIDATION & BENCHMARKS — scripts/
-------------------------------------

  validate_checkpoint.py     certification report (analysis/ci/<model>/)
  benchmark_real_events.py   GWTC events vs dynesty
  dynesty_compare.py         NPE vs dynesty on injections
  inclination_vs_dynesty.py  inclination information vs dynesty (edge-on/face-on)
  polarization_probe.py      information content of the polarization features
  overlap_benchmark.py       overlapping-signal accuracy per rank
  twin_grid.py               twin-injection bias grid → inference/assets/twin_grid.json
  audit_dataset.py           dataset audit (hard failures stop the pipeline)
  run_pipeline.py            unattended cluster pipeline; summarize_runs.py
                             writes the run summary
